From ccbbe7831f40942609c6fa1f9df6e51f1a9a8e1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elpaablo <donopwhile1@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:09:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] sensorservice: Load the OPLUS fusion light engine
 (content-immune ALS)

Port stock ColorOS's SensorServiceExt seam so the prebuilt
libsensorserviceextimpl.so (OPLUS Fusion Light Sensor Next Gen) can
register as android.sensor.light and run its CWB screen-emission
compensation inside our sensorservice:

- OplusFusionExt: dlopen the engine, call createExtendedFactory and
  drive registration via onSensorFound + registerOplusCustomizeSensor
  (vtable-index dispatch, no OPLUS headers), keep the SensorDeviceExt
  for activate routing
- SensorDevice::activate: drive the fusion ext hook like stock so
  activateFusionSensor starts the CWB screenshot monitor
- Export the five AOSP symbols the engine links against and add the
  three OPLUS helpers (hasSensorRecord, onUidIdleForce,
  setSensorStateForTemporarily) plus the SensorServiceExtFactory base

Gated on persist.alpha.fusion_light (default off; set by
vendor/oneplus/fusion). Devices without the prop are unaffected.
